===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|ante|ampte}} {{q|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|ampte}}, {{m|enm|amte}}, {{m|enm|emete}}, {{m|enm|amete}}, from {{inh|en|ang|æmete|ǣmete|t=ant}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*āmaitijā|lit=biting-thing, cutter}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*ē-|t=off, away}} + {{m|gem-pro|*maitaną|t=to cut}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*meh₂y-|t=to cut}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|emmot|t=ant}}, dialectal {{cog|nl|emt}}, {{m|nl|empt||ant}}, {{cog|de|Ameise}} and {{m|de|Emse|t=ant}}. See also {{m|en|emmet}}.

